    para: `<p>It's here. Finally.</p>

<p>The National Board of Examinations in Medical Sciences (NBEMS) announced the schedule for NEET PG 2026. Thousands of postgraduate aspirants now know what they're working toward.</p>

<p>If you're taking NEET PG 2026, stop guessing. The dates are locked. Now it's time to actually prepare.</p>

<p>NBEMS released registration timelines, the exam date, when test cities get announced, when results come out. Everything. Here's what matters.</p>

<h4>NEET PG 2026 Is August 30</h4>

<p>The exam happens on August 30, 2026. Sunday. It's a computer-based test at various centers across India.</p>

<p>You've got a fixed target date now. Time to plan your revision, mocks, final prep.</p>

<h4>Information Bulletin Comes July 1</h4>

<p>NBEMS drops the Information Bulletin on July 1, 2026 at 4:00 PM.</p>

<p>It'll have:</p>

<li>Eligibility criteria</li>
<li>Exam scheme</li>
<li>Fee structure</li>
<li>Instructions</li>
<li>Application process</li>
<li>Documents you need</li>

<p>Read it carefully before you apply. No skimming.</p>

<h4>Registration Window: July 1 to July 21</h4>

<p>Applications open July 1 at 5:00 PM. They close July 21 at 11:55 PM.</p>

<p>Don't wait until the last day. Seriously. Last-minute registrations hit server issues. You might miss the deadline over something stupid.</p>

<p>Apply early. Double-check everything. Then you're done.</p>

<h4>Test City Notification: August 11</h4>

<p>August 11 is when you find out which city your exam center is in. The exact center address comes later with your admit card.</p>

<h4>Result Date: By September 30</h4>

<p>Results drop by September 30, 2026. You download your scorecard from the NBEMS portal once they announce results.</p>

<h4>Important Dates Summary</h4>

<table><tr><th>Event</th><th>Date</th></tr>
<tr><td>Information Bulletin Released</td><td>July 1, 2026 at 4:00 PM</td></tr>
<tr><td>Registration Starts</td><td>July 1, 2026 at 5:00 PM</td></tr>
<tr><td>Registration Closes</td><td>July 21, 2026 at 11:55 PM</td></tr>
<tr><td>Test City Intimation</td><td>August 11, 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>NEET PG 2026 Exam</td><td>August 30, 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Result Declaration</td><td>By September 30, 2026</td></tr>
</table>

<h4>What You Should Do Right Now</h4>

<p>The dates are out. You know when everything happens. Use that.</p>

<p>Here's what matters:</p>

<li>Register as soon as the window opens on July 1</li>
<li>Gather all required documents before you apply</li>
<li>Keep solving mocks and previous year questions</li>
<li>Revise high-yield topics instead of starting new stuff</li>
<li>Watch NBEMS announcements for admit card and exam guidelines</li>

<p>Good planning in the final weeks actually changes your score.</p>

<h4>Final Thoughts</h4>

<p>The schedule is official. NEET PG 2026 happens August 30. You've got a timeline.</p>

<p>Stop worrying about dates. Start using them.</p>

<p>Register on time. Stay updated with NBEMS. Use the remaining weeks for actual focused prep.</p>

<p>The countdown is on. Make every day count.</p>

<h4>FAQs</h4>

<p><b>Q: When is the NEET PG 2026 exam?</b><br/>A: NEET PG 2026 will be conducted on 30 August 2026 (Sunday).</p>

<p><b>Q: When does NEET PG 2026 registration begin?</b><br/>A: The registration window opens on 1 July 2026 at 5:00 PM.</p>

<p><b>Q: What is the last date to apply for NEET PG 2026?</b><br/>A: Candidates can submit their application until 21 July 2026 at 11:55 PM.</p>

<p><b>Q: When will the NEET PG 2026 test city be announced?</b><br/>A: NBEMS will release the test city intimation on 11 August 2026.</p>

<p><b>Q: When is the NEET PG 2026 result expected?</b><br/>A: The NEET PG 2026 result is expected to be declared by 30 September 2026.</p>`,
